    "created_at": "2026-06-04T12:52:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-04T12:52:29Z",
    "body": "> Wait, this selector is _mystifying_. What's with the `*|*` there at the end, that's the super-universal selector, it subsumes the entire rest of the selector. I'm very confused.\n\nI think I figured out why all the other selectors are there, as well as `*|*`. There's this rule right before:\n```css\naddress, blockquote, center, div, figure, figcaption, footer, form, header, hr,\nlegend, listing, main, p, plaintext, pre, summary, xmp, article, aside,\n:heading, hgroup, nav, section, search, table, caption, colgroup, col, thead,\ntbody, tfoot, tr, td, th, dir, dd, dl, dt, menu, ol, ul, li, bdi, output,\n[dir=ltr i], [dir=rtl i], [dir=auto i] {\n  unicode-bidi: isolate; \n}\n```\nWhich is almost the same, except that it also lists `bdi` and `output` and is missing `*|*`.\nIf our rule in question had only the `*|*` selector, it wouldn't have enough specificity to override this prior block.\n\nNo idea if `bdi` and `output` should also be overwritten though.\n\nAlso, since I have now signed my name onto the internet to contribute to HTML, I've re-opened my PR to fix the ordering here: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10780",
